From: prplmesh OpenWrt package
Subject: [PATCH] common: use mbed TLS instead of OpenSSL

prplMesh only needs DH (RFC 3526 group 5), SHA-256, HMAC-SHA256 and
AES-128-CBC for the WSC M1/M2 exchange. Implement them with mbed TLS
(libmbedcrypto), which OpenWrt images usually ship anyway, so the
much larger libopenssl is not needed.

The DH shared secret is now always zero padded to the size of the
prime (192 bytes), as the WSC spec requires for the DHKey (hostapd does
the same). Before, a secret with leading zero bytes was hashed
unpadded and the derived keys did not match the peer.

OpenSSL types are no longer exposed by mapf/common/encryption.h.
---
diff --color -ru a/framework/common/CMakeLists.txt b/framework/common/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/framework/common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/framework/common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -9,11 +9,9 @@
 # mapfcommon sources
 set(sources logger.cpp encryption.cpp utils.cpp hmac_wrapper.cpp)
 
-# We use OpenSSL >=3.0.0 for data encryption
-find_package(OpenSSL 3.0 QUIET)
-if(NOT OpenSSL_FOUND)
-	find_package(OpenSSL 1.1 REQUIRED)
-endif()
+# mbed TLS (libmbedcrypto) is used for data encryption
+find_path(MBEDTLS_INCLUDE_DIR mbedtls/aes.h REQUIRED)
+find_library(MBEDCRYPTO_LIBRARY mbedcrypto REQUIRED)
 
 # Create a single common library
 add_library(mapfcommon ${sources})
@@ -22,13 +20,13 @@
 	PRIVATE 
 		elpp
 		json-c 
-	PUBLIC
-		${OPENSSL_LIBRARIES}
+		${MBEDCRYPTO_LIBRARY}
 )
 target_include_directories(mapfcommon
 	PUBLIC 
 		${PLATFORM_INCLUDE_DIR}
-		${OPENSSL_INCLUDE_DIR}
+	PRIVATE
+		${MBEDTLS_INCLUDE_DIR}
 )
 
 configure_file(
